        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-figure",
      "data": {
        "caption_left": "Fig. 01 · Typeset, Markdown in, PDF out",
        "caption_right": "Private, behind an IP allowlist",
        "tone": "plain",
        "image": {
          "file": "media/typeset-home.png",
          "alt": "Typeset's home page: \"Markdown in. Branded PDF out.\", with three branded documents fanned out beside it"
        },
        "frame": "browser",
        "frame_url": "Typeset"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "01\nTHE *problem*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Proposals and reports matter, but laying them out by hand takes hours, and word processors make them look the same as everyone else's.",
        "background": "tinted"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "02\nHOW IT *works*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Typeset is a small Rust service with one job. It takes Markdown, or a structured JSON document, and sets it with Typst in the right brand: fonts, colours and logo, read from the same brand record my other studio tools use. A title becomes a cover page, each top-level heading opens a numbered section, headings never get left at the foot of a page, and tables, code and callouts stay whole. My planning boards and page designs export through it, so a plan, a scope and a proposal all arrive as the same kind of document.",
        "background": "tinted",
        "eyebrow": "Markdown in, PDF out"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "03\nKEPT *private*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Typeset isn't public. It sits behind an IP allowlist I built into my own server tools: nginx refuses every address that isn't on the list, before a request reaches the app, and the API is rate-limited on top. Any change to the list is checked and tested by nginx before it goes live, so a bad edit can't open it up or take it down.",
        "background": "tinted",
        "eyebrow": "Security"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "eyebrow": "04 · What it makes",
        "title": "PROPOSALS, SCOPES AND *audit reports.*",
        "title_size": "large",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Written scopes and proposals for new projects, planning PDFs from my boards, and audit reports with every finding set out by page. Each one gets a cover, numbered sections, a running head and page numbers, in the brand of whoever it's for.",
        "background": "plain"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "05\nFOR *clients*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Your scope and proposal arrive as a clear, designed document you can share with the people who sign off.",
        "background": "tinted",
        "link_label": "Start a project",
        "link_url": "/start"
      }
